WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.349
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:14.619 --> 00:15.854
It's okay.

3
00:16.621 --> 00:18.823
I will settle everything.

4
00:20.892 --> 00:23.061
Ms. Tabatake! Stop!

5
00:23.128 --> 00:24.295
I love you.

6
00:26.397 --> 00:27.432
Ms. Tabatake!

7
00:53.057 --> 00:55.326
Sorry to come so late at night.

8
00:55.393 --> 00:57.795
There's something I needed to ask you right away.

9
00:59.531 --> 01:02.734
May I ask you about your mom?

10
01:05.737 --> 01:06.638
Uh…

11
01:08.139 --> 01:13.611
She said she was going to your house before she left the hospital, right?

12
01:14.946 --> 01:15.914
Yes.

13
01:15.980 --> 01:19.350
Did she say anything else?

14
01:20.084 --> 01:22.754
Why did she want to go home?

15
01:26.357 --> 01:29.127
Was she different from usual?

16
01:34.832 --> 01:39.537
Mom said, "Once I'm discharged, let's have crab pizza."

17
01:40.805 --> 01:41.940
Okay.

18
01:43.741 --> 01:45.944
What else did she say?

19
01:46.010 --> 01:48.213
Can you leave her alone for today?

20
01:48.880 --> 01:50.348
I'm begging you.

21
01:53.685 --> 01:55.887
Why doesn't Mommy answer the phone?

22
01:57.021 --> 02:00.925
Nono, your aunt is on her way here from Obihiro.

23
02:00.992 --> 02:03.261
When she gets here, we'll talk about--

24
02:03.328 --> 02:06.965
Why not now? Where is Mommy?

25
02:10.868 --> 02:13.071
Who do you want to hear the answer from?

26
02:19.143 --> 02:20.878
Dr. Yoshino.

27
02:38.896 --> 02:42.634
Your mom can't come back.

28
02:46.771 --> 02:48.206
She passed away.

29
02:51.943 --> 02:53.278
She died?

30
02:54.512 --> 02:55.813
Why?

31
02:57.982 --> 02:58.983
Uh…

32
03:02.253 --> 03:03.955
We don't know yet.

33
03:05.757 --> 03:08.426
Are there things even adults don't know?

34
03:09.794 --> 03:12.196
Yes, many.

35
03:12.797 --> 03:15.166
That's why I want you to tell me even the smallest details.

36
03:15.233 --> 03:16.134
Why your mom--

37
03:16.200 --> 03:18.202
Nono, you did nothing wrong.

38
03:20.505 --> 03:26.244
We doctors, the nurses, child welfare workers, and the police,

39
03:26.311 --> 03:28.012
we will all help you.

40
03:30.281 --> 03:31.416
Nono…

41
03:33.151 --> 03:34.319
it's okay.

42
03:35.520 --> 03:37.021
You're not alone.

43
03:44.696 --> 03:46.230
Excuse me.

44
03:46.297 --> 03:47.498
Sorry.

45
03:49.133 --> 03:50.768
My name is Nao.

46
03:51.269 --> 03:53.304
Are you a police officer, sir?

47
03:53.371 --> 03:57.809
No. I work in insurance.

48
03:59.210 --> 04:03.448
When your aunt comes, please give her this.

49
04:04.082 --> 04:05.483
I'll help.

50
04:10.855 --> 04:12.056
Excuse us.

51
04:15.760 --> 04:17.528
-A 24-gauge, please. -Okay.

52
04:18.763 --> 04:22.233
If his oxygen level falls below 94, notify me at once.

53
04:26.504 --> 04:31.075
"It's okay?" Why did I say that to a kid?

54
04:32.944 --> 04:35.213
There's no way things are okay.

55
04:37.548 --> 04:40.218
Why? Damn it!

56
04:57.668 --> 05:00.438
Should I take us home?

57
05:00.505 --> 05:02.106
I'm going back to the station.

58
05:07.545 --> 05:09.547
They take people to hell.

59
05:18.523 --> 05:20.258
My apologies!

60
05:20.324 --> 05:21.592
I'm sorry.

61
05:31.569 --> 05:32.804
Well?

62
05:33.805 --> 05:37.475
There was no suicide note left in her home or in her hospital room.

63
05:38.042 --> 05:39.677
It was probably impulsive.

64
05:40.845 --> 05:42.880
Was it really suicide?

65
05:43.481 --> 05:46.551
There are several witnesses, including you.

66
05:49.053 --> 05:50.788
She was scared.

67
05:50.855 --> 05:55.460
Either Ms. Tabatake or Ms. Aya is the accomplice.

68
05:55.526 --> 05:56.961
150 MILLION YEN

69
05:58.329 --> 06:00.631
We sent her phone to the lab.

70
06:00.698 --> 06:04.035
Also, this, the bottle analysis.

71
06:04.836 --> 06:07.872
Only Nikaido's and Saruwatari's fingerprints.

72
06:07.939 --> 06:09.540
None were Tabatake's.

73
06:09.607 --> 06:11.709
I'm glad we got those prints.

74
06:11.776 --> 06:14.712
We have Tabatake's statement, only the motive is left.

75
06:14.779 --> 06:16.547
-Chief. -What?

76
06:16.614 --> 06:20.418
You said you would question Saruwatari again tomorrow. What time?

77
06:20.485 --> 06:22.420
-Why do you want to know? -I just…

78
06:22.487 --> 06:25.857
Our goal is to make her tell us why she gave Nikaido sleeping pills,

79
06:26.524 --> 06:28.159
that's all, right?

80
06:29.627 --> 06:30.928
Base to all teams.

81
06:30.995 --> 06:34.799
Due to bad weather, today's search has been suspended.

82
06:34.866 --> 06:38.569
We did not find the three missing people or any belongings.

83
06:38.636 --> 06:40.338
Tomorrow, after the weather improves,

84
06:40.404 --> 06:43.040
we'll widen the search below the north cliff.

85
06:43.107 --> 06:44.041
That's all.

86
06:52.149 --> 06:53.217
The sky!

87
06:53.284 --> 06:56.020
Are you Mr. Nao from Zennichi Insurance Research?

88
06:57.288 --> 06:58.623
Who is this?

89
06:59.390 --> 07:01.659
I'm Chika Kato.

90
07:01.726 --> 07:04.295
Motoka Tabatake's older sister.

91
07:07.098 --> 07:09.033
What's your business?

92
07:09.934 --> 07:11.769
I'm Nao.

93
07:12.637 --> 07:15.773
Nono gave me this.

94
07:15.840 --> 07:19.443
I'm handling the insurance investigation for this case.

95
07:20.244 --> 07:22.413
It was so sudden.

96
07:22.480 --> 07:25.283
I didn't know who to talk to or what to talk about.

97
07:26.684 --> 07:30.187
My condolences to you for your loss.

98
07:33.090 --> 07:35.059
Did she have other relatives?

99
07:35.126 --> 07:38.462
Only me. Our parents have passed.

100
07:40.331 --> 07:42.466
I'm sorry to ask…

101
07:44.302 --> 07:48.239
but where will Nono live from now on, and who will watch over her?

102
07:50.374 --> 07:55.379
I want to take her, but my husband is strongly against it.

103
07:56.180 --> 07:58.049
We have three children of our own.

104
08:02.353 --> 08:03.454
Um…

105
08:04.689 --> 08:07.525
I have my sister's life insurance policy.

106
08:08.092 --> 08:12.597
She told me to handle it if something happened during her guide work.

107
08:12.663 --> 08:14.465
Is Nono the beneficiary?

108
08:14.532 --> 08:15.366
Yes.

109
08:15.433 --> 08:16.701
I'll look at it.

110
08:19.870 --> 08:21.372
My husband says…

111
08:22.239 --> 08:25.376
if it's suicide, the insurance won't be paid.

112
08:25.443 --> 08:26.510
Is that true?

113
08:27.645 --> 08:30.848
Depending on the contract, it may not be paid.

114
08:31.449 --> 08:34.151
When would it be paid?

115
08:36.287 --> 08:40.291
We have three kids, and my husband said we can't afford to take care of Nono too.

116
08:40.358 --> 08:41.192
30 MILLION YEN

117
08:42.526 --> 08:44.729
It depends on the contract terms.

118
08:46.597 --> 08:47.632
Okay.

119
08:55.272 --> 08:57.742
Thank you for the nail clipper.

120
08:57.808 --> 08:59.110
You got them for me, right?

121
08:59.176 --> 09:00.244
It was nothing.

122
09:00.311 --> 09:01.812
-Good morning. -Hello.

123
09:01.879 --> 09:03.648
-Good morning. -Excuse me.

124
09:09.253 --> 09:11.622
I heard about Ms. Tabatake.

125
09:12.356 --> 09:14.158
Why did she commit suicide?

126
09:14.659 --> 09:16.093
You said Ms. Tabatake…

127
09:17.261 --> 09:20.598
gave Mr. Nikaido water, right?

128
09:22.633 --> 09:26.737
When he said he wanted water…

129
09:26.804 --> 09:30.374
I have a spare bottle. Give it to Mr. Nikaido.

130
09:31.242 --> 09:35.246
Ms. Tabatake told me to give it to him, so I did.

131
09:43.754 --> 09:45.623
So you're not all bad.

132
09:52.897 --> 09:58.369
Why didn't Ms. Tabatake hand it to him herself?

133
09:59.170 --> 10:02.506
I've heard Mr. Nikaido was irritable, but…

134
10:02.573 --> 10:06.610
From the start, she was avoiding him.

135
10:06.677 --> 10:11.215
Ms. Saruwatari, you've climbed this mountain several times, right?

136
10:11.282 --> 10:12.283
Yes.

137
10:12.349 --> 10:15.786
If someone is falling behind, can you help?

138
10:16.487 --> 10:18.022
Yes! Of course.

139
10:18.089 --> 10:19.690
-Thank you. -Thanks.

140
10:27.665 --> 10:28.733
Mr. Tsugaru?

141
10:29.567 --> 10:31.068
No.

142
10:31.135 --> 10:32.303
Tsugaru?

143
10:32.870 --> 10:36.407
She called him that. I thought she mistook him for someone else.

144
10:36.474 --> 10:37.374
Okay.

145
10:38.642 --> 10:41.045
I heard your daughter is doing better.

146
10:42.113 --> 10:44.248
You should thank me a little.

147
10:48.719 --> 10:50.554
Hey, can you take a photo of me?

148
10:50.621 --> 10:51.789
-Is here okay? -Yes!

149
10:53.791 --> 10:57.194
Does that mean the two knew each other?

150
10:57.261 --> 10:58.329
Hello, sir.

151
10:58.395 --> 10:59.663
-It's possible. -Hey, let's go!

152
11:01.632 --> 11:03.234
Excuse me.

153
11:03.968 --> 11:06.203
I'm Shibasaki from Kitami HQ.

154
11:06.704 --> 11:10.274
Why did she call Mr. Nikaido "Tsugaru"?

155
11:10.341 --> 11:13.043
We should investigate Tabatake and Nikaido's connection.

156
11:13.110 --> 11:14.078
Yes.

157
11:14.145 --> 11:15.179
Detective!

158
11:16.180 --> 11:17.281
Yes?

159
11:17.348 --> 11:19.083
About Ms. Tabatake…

160
11:19.650 --> 11:22.620
She was talking with someone on the phone last night.

161
11:24.455 --> 11:26.223
I won't tell the police.

162
11:29.093 --> 11:33.197
The police believe she felt responsible for what happened during the tour

163
11:33.264 --> 11:37.101
and are investigating the possibility that she drove herself to suicide.

164
11:37.168 --> 11:40.204
Chief, what the heck is with today's press conference?

165
11:40.271 --> 11:42.339
Why did they say she felt responsible?

166
11:42.406 --> 11:44.341
None of us ever said that.

167
11:44.408 --> 11:46.510
The call records, have they been analyzed?

168
11:46.577 --> 11:48.345
No unusual calls.

169
11:48.913 --> 11:53.117
94 percent are calls from family and work, and the rest are sales calls.

170
11:53.951 --> 11:55.286
END OF EXTRACTED DATA

171
11:55.352 --> 11:56.987
This last call

172
11:57.655 --> 12:00.424
is two minutes and ten seconds long.

173
12:00.491 --> 12:04.829
-Is it really a sales number? -The lab says it is.

174
12:05.362 --> 12:07.331
Ms. Tabatake was scared of someone--

175
12:07.398 --> 12:08.966
Why couldn't you stop her from jumping?!

176
12:12.603 --> 12:13.904
-Sorry. -My apologies!

177
12:18.776 --> 12:22.546
Keep investigating Nikaido and his connections.

178
12:22.613 --> 12:23.480
Yes.

179
12:27.585 --> 12:28.919
Thank you.

180
12:31.555 --> 12:34.592
Today is Nikaido's funeral. It's our chance.

181
12:34.658 --> 12:35.726
Let's do what needs doing.

182
12:36.293 --> 12:37.761
CALL, 2 MINUTES 10 SECONDS

183
12:40.531 --> 12:44.768
The number you have dialed is not in service.

184
12:45.569 --> 12:49.907
Please check and dial again.

185
13:15.900 --> 13:18.535
There aren't many mourners.

186
13:18.602 --> 13:20.404
Does he not have a lot of friends?

187
13:21.138 --> 13:22.740
My funeral would be like this.

188
13:22.806 --> 13:24.742
Don't say that.

189
13:29.947 --> 13:31.482
That guy again.

190
13:31.548 --> 13:32.583
Yes.

191
13:34.985 --> 13:36.553
Hello.

192
13:40.090 --> 13:41.558
Here.

193
13:41.625 --> 13:43.861
I'll give you the receipt later.

194
13:46.730 --> 13:51.001
Didn't you say you didn't want to see my face?

195
13:51.068 --> 13:54.571
I changed my mind. Sorry for calling you over so suddenly.

196
14:02.146 --> 14:05.649
Is insurance murder a grave crime?

197
14:10.487 --> 14:13.290
The motive is vicious, you know.

198
14:14.291 --> 14:17.428
Even with just one victim, a death sentence can happen.

199
14:17.494 --> 14:19.163
You've already decided that

200
14:19.997 --> 14:23.267
I killed my husband for the insurance, right?

201
14:23.334 --> 14:26.370
Finding that out is the police's job.

202
14:26.437 --> 14:31.675
My job is to gather material to decide whether the insurance should be paid.

203
14:31.742 --> 14:34.678
The insurance company decides, not me.

204
14:35.245 --> 14:36.213
Yes.

205
14:36.780 --> 14:40.351
The company will decide based on your investigation?

206
14:40.417 --> 14:46.457
I believe insurance should be paid justly, not one yen more or less.

207
14:46.523 --> 14:48.826
-That's how I investigate-- -What do you want to ask?

208
14:53.530 --> 14:54.832
Two months ago,

209
14:55.366 --> 14:59.937
when Mr. Nikaido's insurance was raised to 150 million yen.

210
15:02.106 --> 15:04.908
Whose decision was it?

211
15:08.412 --> 15:09.313
My husband's.

212
15:09.980 --> 15:11.849
He decided the amount too.

213
15:11.915 --> 15:14.651
Do you know why he raised it?

214
15:16.887 --> 15:18.856
It was our tenth wedding anniversary.

215
15:21.291 --> 15:23.694
When I was 48,

216
15:24.828 --> 15:28.165
he was only 34, and proposed to me.

217
15:31.035 --> 15:34.471
I thought he would soon switch to a young girl.

218
15:37.307 --> 15:39.576
But he stayed my husband for ten years.

219
15:41.512 --> 15:42.780
So…

220
15:44.615 --> 15:48.385
instead of promising to stay with me until death,

221
15:50.154 --> 15:52.523
he rewrote the contract.

222
15:57.294 --> 16:00.931
Did you love Mr. Nikaido?

223
16:08.172 --> 16:09.673
I loved him.

224
16:13.010 --> 16:17.714
I was physically, mentally, and financially

225
16:19.416 --> 16:21.185
satisfied with him.

226
16:27.758 --> 16:29.726
I'm lonely without him.

227
16:34.098 --> 16:37.568
Thank you for waiting. Here are his ashes.

228
16:50.814 --> 16:52.783
I understand.

229
16:54.985 --> 16:57.187
I know this is a tough time for you,

230
16:58.288 --> 17:01.925
but may I check your financial situation?

231
17:03.861 --> 17:04.862
Yes.

232
17:22.846 --> 17:26.617
There's testimony that Teruyuki Nikaido and Tabatake knew each other.

233
17:26.683 --> 17:29.720
Tabatake called Nikaido "Tsugaru,"

234
17:29.786 --> 17:33.123
and Nikaido seemed to know Tabatake had a daughter.

235
17:33.190 --> 17:34.925
Whose testimony was that?

236
17:34.992 --> 17:36.126
Saruwatari's.

237
17:38.962 --> 17:41.398
Didn't this come out in the questioning?

238
17:41.465 --> 17:43.066
-What are you getting at? -Ogoma!

239
17:44.101 --> 17:45.836
Don't criticize another squad's work.

240
17:46.970 --> 17:48.005
My apologies.

241
17:49.907 --> 17:52.309
We looked into Saruwatari's finances.

242
17:53.310 --> 17:55.746
She's about four million yen in debt.

243
17:58.382 --> 18:00.083
About the sleeping pill…

244
18:00.150 --> 18:05.155
Saruwatari's father, who died last year, was prescribed Zolpidem for insomnia.

245
18:05.756 --> 18:07.257
That settles it.

246
18:10.961 --> 18:13.697
Kitami HQ will be calling the shots.

247
18:15.432 --> 18:16.900
-That's all. -Yes, sir!

248
18:21.338 --> 18:22.906
Ogoma, you…

249
18:22.973 --> 18:24.141
Officer Ogoma.

250
18:24.942 --> 18:25.609
Yes?

251
18:27.411 --> 18:30.280
Won't you help with the investigation?

252
18:32.883 --> 18:33.850
I will!

253
18:36.420 --> 18:39.556
Oh, my! Did he do it?

254
18:39.623 --> 18:42.192
You were Saruwatari's student, right?

255
18:42.259 --> 18:45.495
She was only a temp teacher though.

256
18:45.562 --> 18:47.431
Saruwatari denies the charge.

257
18:47.497 --> 18:48.632
Hello.

258
18:48.699 --> 18:50.067
Hello.

259
18:50.133 --> 18:52.869
We have physical evidence and Tabatake's testimony.

260
18:52.936 --> 18:56.840
But the other tour guests are missing. We can't back up Tabatake's testimony.

261
18:57.374 --> 19:00.244
It's a hard case, but for the late Mr. Nikaido,

262
19:00.310 --> 19:03.180
we want to give it a murder indictment.

263
19:05.315 --> 19:07.751
So what should I do?

264
19:09.853 --> 19:11.989
Get a confession from Saruwatari.

265
19:13.957 --> 19:16.560
Find out what she did on that mountain and where.

266
19:22.899 --> 19:25.469
I hear you've asked to be transferred to another station.

267
19:25.535 --> 19:26.603
Yes.

268
19:30.941 --> 19:31.975
I've asked many times.

269
19:32.042 --> 19:35.178
If you get the confession, I'll recommend you to your preferred station.

270
19:36.346 --> 19:37.347
Huh?

271
19:39.816 --> 19:41.551
Do your best.

272
20:03.373 --> 20:04.508
Ms. Aya.

273
20:09.446 --> 20:10.814
What's wrong?

274
20:13.917 --> 20:15.585
-No-- -Sit down.

275
20:20.624 --> 20:25.062
They've already decided I'm the culprit, haven't they?

276
20:26.029 --> 20:28.231
What did they tell you during questioning?

277
20:28.965 --> 20:32.736
Who are those people? They even brought up my debt.

278
20:37.007 --> 20:38.241
What debt?

279
20:39.142 --> 20:43.046
My useless father's gambling debt.

280
20:44.214 --> 20:47.951
He tricked many people and borrowed money everywhere.

281
20:49.119 --> 20:50.721
I'm paying it back.

282
20:51.288 --> 20:53.290
Did you explain that to the officers?

283
20:53.357 --> 20:54.391
I did.

284
20:54.958 --> 20:56.226
I did, but…

285
20:56.293 --> 20:59.463
Do they even want to listen?

286
21:01.198 --> 21:04.601
I hadn't seen my father in years.

287
21:05.535 --> 21:08.939
I didn't even know he got sleeping pills at the hospital.

288
21:10.207 --> 21:11.808
As for Mr. Nikaido,

289
21:11.875 --> 21:16.480
I don't even know who he is or what he does.

290
21:17.013 --> 21:18.782
No matter how many times I say I don't know,

291
21:18.849 --> 21:22.819
they say, "Think harder," or "A little digging will tell us."

292
21:25.622 --> 21:28.024
How can I make them believe me?

293
21:31.695 --> 21:35.766
Their job is to doubt suspects.

294
21:41.571 --> 21:44.875
If you say Mr. Nikaido was killed,

295
21:44.941 --> 21:49.012
I want you to find the culprit. That's why I'm cooperating with the police.

296
21:49.079 --> 21:51.848
Sorry for the trouble.

297
21:54.751 --> 21:58.855
I never imagined you would become a police officer.

298
22:00.590 --> 22:01.591
Well…

299
22:02.225 --> 22:03.727
It just kind of happened.

300
22:05.495 --> 22:09.399
It's a job that helps the world and people.

301
22:10.801 --> 22:13.336
It's not that great.

302
22:13.403 --> 22:15.605
It is! You're doing well.

303
22:23.246 --> 22:25.248
What do you really want to know?

304
22:28.585 --> 22:30.120
The truth…

305
22:30.854 --> 22:33.523
about what happened on the mountain.

306
22:40.497 --> 22:46.036
Do you also think I gave Mr. Nikaido the sleeping pill?

307
22:50.874 --> 22:52.275
Did you?

308
22:54.077 --> 22:55.178
What do you think?

309
23:04.187 --> 23:07.491
You don't know? I guess you don't know me very well.

310
23:08.024 --> 23:10.927
Won't you tell me?

311
23:19.202 --> 23:20.203
I…

312
23:24.674 --> 23:26.042
I didn't do it.

313
23:26.776 --> 23:28.211
I didn't.

314
23:28.278 --> 23:30.013
The culprit is…

315
23:31.147 --> 23:32.649
someone else.

316
23:43.894 --> 23:45.428
-Hello. -Hello.

317
23:45.495 --> 23:47.430
-Good work. -Hello, sir.

318
23:47.497 --> 23:50.634
Do you think Saruwatari really did it?

319
23:52.035 --> 23:55.171
As long as there's evidence, we'll consider her a suspect.

320
23:57.674 --> 23:58.975
Mr. Endo.

321
24:28.371 --> 24:30.340
Hey! Ogoma, you're home.

322
24:30.407 --> 24:31.975
Hello.

323
24:32.042 --> 24:33.209
Whoa!

324
24:34.177 --> 24:36.813
I made progress today!

325
24:36.880 --> 24:41.117
-I finally had a serious talk with Harune. -I'm glad.

326
24:41.184 --> 24:43.687
From my position on the insurance side…

327
24:44.554 --> 24:45.822
Is your stomach hurting?

328
24:47.324 --> 24:48.758
Ogoma.

329
24:51.127 --> 24:53.063
Why are you coming in?

330
24:53.129 --> 24:55.031
I want to tell you a few things.

331
24:55.098 --> 24:56.166
Not today.

332
24:56.232 --> 24:57.300
That hurts.

333
24:58.368 --> 25:02.973
In my investigation, Harune has no link to the others.

334
25:03.039 --> 25:06.409
The increase in the insurance coverage has a reasonable cause.

335
25:07.043 --> 25:10.981
Since I can't find any evidence that Harune, the beneficiary,

336
25:11.047 --> 25:15.185
was involved in Mr. Nikaido's death, my insurance investigation must end.

337
25:16.119 --> 25:17.320
You're really ending it?

338
25:17.387 --> 25:21.858
Our time together was short, but I learned a lot from you.

339
25:22.525 --> 25:25.729
We still don't know why Mr. Nikaido died!

340
25:25.795 --> 25:29.899
Finding the culprit is a job for you police, not me.

341
25:32.936 --> 25:35.438
But Ms. Tabatake is dead too.

342
25:38.808 --> 25:40.810
Wasn't it a suicide?

343
25:40.877 --> 25:42.045
It's under investigation.

344
25:44.180 --> 25:45.482
Let's eat.

345
25:49.586 --> 25:50.520
Let's eat.

346
25:54.491 --> 25:57.160
With the insurance Ms. Tabatake had

347
25:58.161 --> 26:01.097
if she died, 30 million yen would go to Nono.

348
26:01.164 --> 26:05.602
The contract was made two years ago. If it's suicide, the money isn't paid.

349
26:06.936 --> 26:07.904
What?

350
26:09.239 --> 26:13.243
I mean, what if someone took out insurance with the intention to kill themselves?

351
26:13.309 --> 26:15.512
They won't pay for a contract made within two or three years.

352
26:17.047 --> 26:20.250
What happens to Nono then?

353
26:22.619 --> 26:23.653
Would Ms. Tabatake

354
26:24.688 --> 26:28.425
really throw away 30 million yen that she could give her daughter?

355
26:28.491 --> 26:31.695
-Money again-- -Nothing is more certain than money.

356
26:32.462 --> 26:36.299
So, for now, this is the police's theory, right?

357
26:36.366 --> 26:38.368
TOUR GUESTS

358
26:39.169 --> 26:45.408
Ms. Aya gave Mr. Nikaido sleeping pills and killed him.

359
26:45.475 --> 26:46.976
Yes, that's about it.

360
26:47.610 --> 26:50.146
And your theory, Ogoma, is this.

361
26:50.213 --> 26:55.285
Ms. Tabatake gave Mr. Nikaido the pills and killed him.

362
26:55.351 --> 26:59.889
Also, Ms. Tabatake was scared of someone.

363
26:59.956 --> 27:00.757
Who?

364
27:02.358 --> 27:03.193
Someone.

365
27:05.628 --> 27:06.730
Just "someone."

366
27:08.364 --> 27:10.834
"Someone."

367
27:11.634 --> 27:15.572
-Which one do you think it is? -I don't care much anymore.

368
27:15.638 --> 27:17.373
You should care!

369
27:17.440 --> 27:19.776
Ms. Tabatake did many unnatural things.

370
27:19.843 --> 27:22.946
Like changing the beneficiary on the hiking insurance.

371
27:23.012 --> 27:25.548
A mistake like that would be a huge problem.

372
27:27.617 --> 27:28.651
Detective…

373
27:28.718 --> 27:29.786
She did say that.

374
27:29.853 --> 27:32.188
If she made a mistake it would be a big problem.

375
27:33.189 --> 27:35.759
Something like that could easily get her fired.

376
27:35.825 --> 27:40.263
Changing it wouldn't get her the insurance money either. So why take that risk?

377
27:40.330 --> 27:43.032
Would she take such a high risk?

378
27:43.099 --> 27:44.801
The fingerprints too.

379
27:44.868 --> 27:46.903
Ms. Tabatake's didn’t show up?

380
27:48.838 --> 27:50.273
If Ms. Aya were the culprit,

381
27:50.340 --> 27:53.143
I don't think she would be so careless as to leave prints.

382
27:53.209 --> 27:56.179
Even discounting your bias for Ms. Aya,

383
27:56.246 --> 27:59.349
I agree that Ms. Tabatake's actions look unnatural.

384
28:02.852 --> 28:06.823
If the three missing people were alive,

385
28:06.890 --> 28:10.426
we would know who is telling the truth.

386
28:13.763 --> 28:17.534
There's a record of a person lost in the Andes

387
28:17.600 --> 28:20.403
who was rescued after 72 days.

388
28:21.437 --> 28:22.539
That long?

389
28:22.605 --> 28:25.441
Mt. Shikara isn't as harsh as the Andes.

390
28:25.508 --> 28:28.545
If they're alive, they would have come down by now.

391
28:31.648 --> 28:32.916
-Chief. -Yeah?

392
28:33.483 --> 28:34.851
Can I be of help?

393
28:36.519 --> 28:37.921
If I can, please tell me.

394
28:37.987 --> 28:39.022
Yes.

395
28:55.104 --> 28:57.841
HQ wants to pin it on Saruwatari.

396
28:58.575 --> 29:00.176
Here, look at these too.

397
29:00.743 --> 29:04.013
I can't believe I got such a messy case right before retirement.

398
29:04.080 --> 29:07.951
We're usually called for drunks fighting.

399
29:08.017 --> 29:09.919
-Right? -Yes.

400
29:09.986 --> 29:11.754
Only small cases like those.

401
29:11.821 --> 29:13.189
True.

402
29:15.191 --> 29:19.495
I've been waiting for a big case too.

403
29:22.832 --> 29:24.300
Mr. Awashima,

404
29:26.502 --> 29:31.474
have you ever disagreed with the higher-ups' plans?

405
29:33.676 --> 29:34.577
A few times.

406
29:35.845 --> 29:38.781
-Think they ever got a wrong lead? -Yes.

407
29:40.583 --> 29:42.285
What did you do then?

408
29:47.090 --> 29:50.660
Followed the higher-ups' plan. That's what officers do.

409
30:08.278 --> 30:09.279
Hello.

410
30:12.715 --> 30:13.716
Hello?

411
30:14.484 --> 30:16.519
-Can you hear me? -I can.

412
30:17.587 --> 30:20.123
Who is this?

413
30:20.189 --> 30:23.426
I'm Nono Tabatake. I want to ask you something.

414
30:26.996 --> 30:30.033
-You… want to ask me? -Yes.

415
30:39.709 --> 30:40.877
-Hello. -Hello.

416
30:40.944 --> 30:42.912
-Please use the sanitizer. -Okay.

417
30:45.081 --> 30:47.116
Brushing her teeth?

418
30:51.888 --> 30:55.191
I brought a get-well gift. The doctor said it's okay.

419
30:59.929 --> 31:01.564
Here you go.

420
31:02.298 --> 31:06.502
Canned soup, warmed up. It's hot, so be careful.

421
31:06.569 --> 31:08.037
Let's eat.

422
31:08.871 --> 31:11.341
Drinking this on a snowy mountain…

423
31:11.407 --> 31:13.876
It makes you feel alive.

424
31:19.849 --> 31:21.818
Better not talk about mountains.

425
31:29.425 --> 31:32.028
Okay, ask. I'm all ears.

426
31:33.096 --> 31:33.997
Okay.

427
31:34.564 --> 31:37.900
How much money does it take to live alone?

428
31:41.270 --> 31:43.906
You mean you, by yourself?

429
31:43.973 --> 31:47.243
When I leave the hospital, I want to go back to the house where I lived with Mom.

430
31:55.351 --> 31:57.587
Is it impossible for me?

431
32:04.427 --> 32:05.461
Listen,

432
32:06.796 --> 32:07.964
Japan…

433
32:09.232 --> 32:13.803
has a rule that children in trouble must not be left alone,

434
32:13.870 --> 32:16.873
and adults must protect them.

435
32:16.939 --> 32:18.908
-A rule? -Yes.

436
32:18.975 --> 32:21.244
It's called child welfare.

437
32:23.746 --> 32:27.250
My mom has life insurance, right?

438
32:27.316 --> 32:28.651
She does.

439
32:29.786 --> 32:33.723
My mom never gets involved in dangerous trips.

440
32:33.790 --> 32:37.326
Dangerous trips make more money,

441
32:37.393 --> 32:40.830
but she doesn't do them because she always wants to come home.

442
32:45.068 --> 32:47.303
That’s a wonderful decision.

443
32:49.338 --> 32:51.607
"If Mommy is gone,

444
32:51.674 --> 32:54.444
I'll leave enough money so you won't be in trouble.

445
32:54.510 --> 32:56.746
Don't worry." She told me so.

446
32:57.647 --> 33:00.783
Can I live alone on that money?

447
33:09.892 --> 33:11.027
Your mom

448
33:13.296 --> 33:15.465
really loved you.

449
33:27.610 --> 33:30.046
All of her life insurance money

450
33:31.581 --> 33:35.017
is proof of her love.

451
33:39.889 --> 33:44.794
Okay, I got it. I'm now your personal advisor.

452
33:49.699 --> 33:51.934
If you have any questions, you can ask me.

453
33:55.838 --> 33:57.273
Was my Mommy…

454
33:59.242 --> 34:01.110
killed?

455
34:05.882 --> 34:07.383
Why do you think so?

456
34:10.019 --> 34:13.556
Was your mom being targeted by someone scary?

457
34:18.394 --> 34:20.530
How old is Ms. Tabatake's daughter?

458
34:20.596 --> 34:23.232
She's eight, she's in third grade.

459
34:23.299 --> 34:25.735
Any relatives to take her in?

460
34:25.801 --> 34:28.271
There are, but it looks tough.

461
34:28.337 --> 34:31.174
So she'll go to an orphanage.

462
34:31.240 --> 34:36.112
She says she wants to live alone in her old home.

463
34:39.682 --> 34:43.419
Nao, if an eight-year-old girl

464
34:43.486 --> 34:47.890
said she wanted to live alone, would you say "go ahead"?

465
34:47.957 --> 34:52.295
No way. I wouldn’t allow something that dangerous.

466
34:52.361 --> 34:56.199
Yes. She still needs someone to care for her.

467
35:09.879 --> 35:12.915
I can't object to that.

468
35:14.483 --> 35:15.751
But is there a way to--

469
35:15.818 --> 35:19.655
Is this relevant? You're being distracted.

470
35:19.722 --> 35:23.993
I'm not. I'm heading to Harune's place.

471
35:24.060 --> 35:26.395
To see her financial records.

472
35:41.711 --> 35:43.212
Can I get another speeding ticket?

473
35:43.279 --> 35:45.348
You know I would never say yes.

474
35:45.414 --> 35:49.051
Wait, Harune! Wait!

475
35:49.118 --> 35:50.620
Wait!

476
35:51.621 --> 35:53.356
How is it? Will you be done today?

477
35:53.990 --> 35:56.259
Ogoma, you can return to normal duty after tomorrow.

478
35:56.325 --> 35:58.894
-Why? -Because we want you to.

479
35:58.961 --> 36:00.830
Is it because I know the suspect?

480
36:00.896 --> 36:02.999
I already told you. She's an old acquaintance!

481
36:03.065 --> 36:04.567
It's a decided matter.

482
36:04.634 --> 36:07.903
I have to ask Harune why Ms. Tabatake called Nikaido "Tsugaru".

483
36:07.970 --> 36:09.538
-Please. Take care. -Chief.

484
36:09.605 --> 36:10.806
Bye!

485
36:10.873 --> 36:12.341
-Bye. -Chief.

486
36:13.442 --> 36:15.778
-You want to be promoted, don't you? -Yes.

487
36:15.845 --> 36:17.780
This time, stay out of it.

488
36:18.681 --> 36:19.982
Don't get involved.

489
36:22.118 --> 36:25.788
Mr. Awashima, you think something is off too, don't you?

490
36:25.855 --> 36:28.958
Tabatake, the center of the case, suddenly died,

491
36:29.025 --> 36:31.127
and the next day, it was already judged a suicide.

492
36:31.193 --> 36:32.995
Even though there's no suicide note.

493
36:33.562 --> 36:37.199
No information about Nikaido's wife or the other tour guests

494
36:37.266 --> 36:39.402
has been provided by the higher-ups.

495
36:40.970 --> 36:43.205
Are the higher-ups hiding something?

496
36:43.272 --> 36:47.043
They say the search for the missing might end tomorrow.

497
36:47.109 --> 36:48.444
They're ending it?

498
36:48.511 --> 36:50.313
Enough. Don't get involved.

499
36:51.514 --> 36:52.682
Trust me on this.

500
36:53.249 --> 36:55.451
Mr. Awashima and Masaru.

501
36:55.518 --> 36:57.119
-Yes. -The two of you…

502
36:58.087 --> 36:59.689
It's over!

503
36:59.755 --> 37:00.956
I was so stupid!

504
37:01.757 --> 37:02.925
Tsugaru?

505
37:02.992 --> 37:04.360
She called him that.

506
37:04.427 --> 37:05.361
150 MILLION YEN

507
37:10.366 --> 37:12.201
Doubt everything.

508
37:13.169 --> 37:17.206
Once you have doubted everything, what remains is the truth.

509
37:18.674 --> 37:20.343
Call me.

510
37:20.409 --> 37:22.578
-On my phone. -I'm leaving first.

511
37:27.516 --> 37:28.751
What is it?

512
37:28.818 --> 37:29.952
Harune got away!

513
37:30.019 --> 37:31.087
What?

514
37:31.153 --> 37:34.056
I was fooled. I was stupid to trust her.

515
37:34.123 --> 37:36.158
What are you talking about? Where did she go?

516
37:36.225 --> 37:37.159
Probably Tokyo.

517
37:37.226 --> 37:39.161
-Why Tokyo? -I knew it.

518
37:39.228 --> 37:40.830
That woman is suspicious.

519
37:41.530 --> 37:44.300
Who benefits when Mr. Nikaido dies?

520
37:44.867 --> 37:46.902
Harune, of course.

521
37:46.969 --> 37:49.305
She ran because she knows something?

522
37:49.372 --> 37:51.173
-I'll find her and make her confess. -No.

523
37:51.240 --> 37:53.776
-What? -Us police will catch her first.

524
37:56.579 --> 37:58.147
-I'll be first. -No!

525
37:58.214 --> 38:00.316
I'll find her and make her talk right away.

526
38:00.383 --> 38:02.184
Tell me the details.

527
38:03.085 --> 38:04.587
-Ogoma! -Yes?

528
38:04.653 --> 38:06.322
Want to go for a drink?

529
38:06.389 --> 38:10.025
I'm going home. I'm taking leave tomorrow.

530
38:10.526 --> 38:12.228
Okay! I'm off!

531
38:13.963 --> 38:16.832
You don’t need to take leave for this.

532
38:24.840 --> 38:26.208
It's Ogoma.

533
38:27.276 --> 38:29.178
Don't admit to what you didn't do.

534
38:36.252 --> 38:39.088
WE WON'T BE ABLE TO MEET FOR A WHILE HANG ON UNTIL I GET BACK

535
38:59.809 --> 39:01.343
Thank you for waiting.

536
39:01.410 --> 39:06.248
Japan Airlines to Tokyo Haneda, departing at 9:50 a.m.

537
39:06.315 --> 39:08.083
Wait for me. I'll catch you, Harune.

538
39:08.651 --> 39:10.286
-So cool. -Are you making fun of me?

539
39:10.352 --> 39:12.221
-I am. -Huh?

540
39:12.288 --> 39:14.056
-Just kidding. -Try again, please.

541
39:14.123 --> 39:14.957
Here.

542
39:15.024 --> 39:16.025
Try again.

543
39:16.091 --> 39:17.526
-What are you doing? -I'm…

544
39:25.234 --> 39:28.204
-Gather all the CCTV data you can. -Yes.

545
39:28.270 --> 39:31.106
-If they refuse, persuade them. -We've arrived!

546
39:31.173 --> 39:32.575
This way.

547
39:32.641 --> 39:35.611
Ogoma, this way.

548
39:36.612 --> 39:38.614
Do we have anything to cool him down?

549
39:38.681 --> 39:39.682
I'll go look.

550
39:39.748 --> 39:41.684
-Nao! -How are you doing?

551
39:41.750 --> 39:43.052
Who is that?

552
39:43.118 --> 39:45.654
-A detective from Hokkaido. -Who hurt him?

553
39:46.222 --> 39:47.623
No one.

554
39:52.194 --> 39:53.028
Huh?

555
39:53.596 --> 39:54.730
Mr. Nao?

556
39:54.797 --> 39:56.131
Where are you, Ogoma?

557
39:56.198 --> 39:58.033
In front of the station.

558
39:58.100 --> 39:59.735
What do you see?

559
39:59.802 --> 40:01.670
Lots of people.

560
40:01.737 --> 40:02.671
There you are.

561
40:02.738 --> 40:04.807
Where were you going?

562
40:09.578 --> 40:11.080
Wow!

563
40:18.754 --> 40:20.055
First time in Tokyo?

564
40:21.090 --> 40:24.226
Yes. It's so humid!

565
40:24.293 --> 40:29.231
He's worn out by the crowds. His place in Hokkaido is really remote.

566
40:29.298 --> 40:30.699
Don’t push yourself. Rest.

567
40:30.766 --> 40:31.800
No, I'm fine.

568
40:32.501 --> 40:34.970
-Any idea where Harune went? -Yes.

569
40:35.037 --> 40:37.406
Nikaido owns a condo in Shibuya.

570
40:37.473 --> 40:38.307
Shibuya?

571
40:38.374 --> 40:39.909
-I gotta go-- -Rest!

572
40:39.975 --> 40:41.076
Okay.

573
40:41.143 --> 40:45.481
I'll send you security camera footage from around the condo. Check all of it.

574
40:46.181 --> 40:47.216
I have to do it?

575
40:47.283 --> 40:49.685
Of course. Hurry up.

576
40:49.752 --> 40:51.220
Find Harune already.

577
40:51.287 --> 40:55.291
I don't want to pay 150 million yen to that shady woman!

578
40:58.060 --> 41:00.462
How many hours of footage are there?

579
41:01.196 --> 41:02.431
Don't force yourself.

580
41:02.498 --> 41:05.100
No, I'm okay.

581
41:06.735 --> 41:07.703
All right.

582
41:08.571 --> 41:11.907
How is Ms. Aya doing?

583
41:11.974 --> 41:14.276
The police interrogate her every day.

584
41:14.343 --> 41:15.678
Figures.

585
41:15.744 --> 41:17.646
I don't know anything anymore.

586
41:18.347 --> 41:21.850
About what's true and who's lying.

587
41:21.917 --> 41:25.921
Honestly, I only learned about murder cases at the police academy.

588
41:28.257 --> 41:31.927
I lost Harune because I couldn't doubt her.

589
41:31.994 --> 41:35.464
I should've doubted her before trusting her.

590
41:35.531 --> 41:37.366
Doubt everything.

591
41:37.433 --> 41:38.734
Exactly.

592
41:42.871 --> 41:44.373
Ogoma.

593
41:44.440 --> 41:47.676
-Yes? -Right now, who do you doubt the most?

594
41:50.546 --> 41:51.647
The police.

595
41:55.751 --> 41:57.853
You shouldn't say that as a police officer.

596
41:59.788 --> 42:02.791
You overturned police investigations before, right?

597
42:03.525 --> 42:05.761
Yeah. The Hakodate case?

598
42:05.828 --> 42:07.429
Or the Sapporo one?

599
42:11.533 --> 42:13.235
The investigation was sloppy.

600
42:14.303 --> 42:16.438
The higher-ups wanted to hide their mistake

601
42:16.505 --> 42:18.540
and bent the facts to do it.

602
42:19.041 --> 42:23.379
That was a long time ago.

603
42:27.316 --> 42:29.418
May I tell an old story too?

604
42:31.387 --> 42:33.222
-Sure. -Here goes.

605
42:35.290 --> 42:39.028
In my hometown, innocent people were often arrested.

606
42:39.094 --> 42:41.664
Your hometown had no laws or justice.

607
42:42.898 --> 42:46.802
I thought the police were trash, so I joined the police.

608
42:47.936 --> 42:50.439
That's a rare reason to join.

609
42:51.774 --> 42:56.812
I figured if I joined the police, I could make the world more peaceful.

610
42:58.380 --> 43:00.382
And then? What happened?

611
43:06.722 --> 43:07.690
Ogoma?

612
43:09.525 --> 43:10.359
Harune?

613
43:11.627 --> 43:13.328
Not her. That's a man.

614
43:14.730 --> 43:15.731
Who?

615
43:16.699 --> 43:18.233
Is that Mr. Monden?

616
43:18.300 --> 43:20.069
-Ryutaro Monden? -Yes.

617
43:20.135 --> 43:22.971
-The missing guy? Wait! -Yes.

618
43:23.038 --> 43:25.074
Is it him? Or someone who looks like him?

619
43:25.140 --> 43:27.509
-Why? -Be quiet! Give me a moment!

620
43:28.143 --> 43:29.111
Here.

621
